# Assistant content: markdown while it streams. The live block renders the
# reply's markdown as it arrives (internal/tui/streammd.go), so a reply
# stopped partway, mid bold phrase, already shows its heading, bullet and
# bold text rendered, with no raw "##" or "**" on screen, and nothing
# reformats when the block commits.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/content-streaming-markdown.yaml
@size 120x40

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
SHOT welcome
TYPE explain the change
KEY enter
WAITFOR /per-user bucket that refills/ 20
SHOT mid-stream
EXPECT /Rate limiter/
EXPECT /• each request takes a token/
EXPECT_NOT /##|\*\*/
EXPECT /▍/
RELEASE rest
WAITFOR /Nothing else in the upload path changed/ 20
SHOT reply-committed
EXPECT /Rate limiter/
EXPECT /limiter := NewBucket/
EXPECT_NOT /##|\*\*|```/
EXPECT_NOT /▍/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
